# No hacky workarounds

Do not ship brittle patches as the primary fix. This site is hand-authored
HTML and CSS. That is the architecture, not something to fight.

Acceptable when narrow, explained, and based on stable CSS/HTML:

- semantic markup and one or two stylesheets
- CSS custom properties from the blueprint tokens
- a few dozen lines of optional home JS (easter egg, footer year)

Stop when the only path is:

- adding a framework, Tailwind, or a design-system kit to “look finished”
- overlay divs, z-index wars, or covering GitHub Pages chrome
- timing-based retries, layout thrash, or JS that the page needs to render
- analytics or third-party widgets “just while we debug”
- copying `resources/` binaries straight into Pages without crop/export

## Instead: hand-off writeup

Create `docs/handoffs/YYYYMMDD_<topic-slug>.md` so another session can
research (CSS, Pages, accessibility), consider alternatives, and implement a
proper fix. Follow `.cursor/rules/handoff-documents.mdc`.
